  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday morning through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1250 PM EST Wed Nov 18 2026\n\nThe extended periods begin Fri morning with GA positioned between\na high pressure over the Mid-Atlantic and 2 low pressure centers \nwith one over the northeastern Gulf and the second developing just\noff the South FL Atlantic coast. The ridge to the north is \nweakening a bit as its center moves NE Fri allowing moisture to \ncontinue to spread into south and central GA Georgia. Both the GFS\nand ECMWF keep the deep layered moisture and better dynamics \nsouth of the area but we could still see come isolated to \nscattered showers across central GA Fri and Sat. WPC has put east \ncentral GA under an Excessive Rain Outlook (ERO) for Fri and Sat. \nPrecipitable water values are expected in the 1\" to 1.5\" range \nacross central GA Fri/Sat. \n\nDuring the day Fri the low center just off the S FL Atlantic \ncoast begins to develop becoming the dominant low center. This low\nis expected to deepen fairly substantially through Sat morning as\nit moves North to just east of the GA coast. Both the GFS and \nECMWF show this low center continuing to develop through the \nweekend as it moves up the eastern seaboard. The models show minor\ndifferences in timing and location but they both show it becoming\na very vigorous storm as it moves NE through day 7. Drier air on \nthe back side of this low and a mid-level ridge traversing the \nSoutheast is anticipated to promote benign weather Sunday and \nMonday. For now the biggest issue we see with this developing low \ncenter is the tightening pressure gradient between the low and the\nridge will drive breezy easterly winds across the forecast area \nFri night and Saturday.\n\nLow level moisture and increased cloud cover will contribute to \nlow temperatures in the upper 40s to mid 50s each morning over the\nweekend and into the early parts of next week. These lows will be\nbetween 5 to 10 degrees above seasonal norms. Low temps do begin \nto cool to near normal by day 7. High temperatures will largely be\nin the upper 60s to 70s each afternoon.",
